  "description": "Michigan's 1st Congressional District, encompassing the entire Upper Peninsula and northern Lower Peninsula (roughly 44% of the state's landmass), is an R+13 district. Incumbent Republican Rep. Jack Bergman, first elected in 2016 and a retired Marine Corps lieutenant general, is seeking a sixth term. The Democratic primary features three candidates \u2014 Callie Barr (an attorney and veteran advocate who was the 2024 nominee), architect and Iron Mountain city councilmember Kyle Blomquist, and industrial designer Wayne Stiles. Bergman faces two primary challengers from the right, Matthew DenOtter and Justin Michal. Independent candidate Zebulon Featherly is also running in the general election. The primary will be held on August 4, 2026.",
